x86_64-linux  Three cxx1-only names and one difference behind them, the one docs/CONFORMANCE.md records as "an inline member function is a strong symbol": `_ZNK1S5twiceEv` and `_ZN1QC1Ei` are defined inside their classes and cxx1 emits an ordinary definition where clang emits them linkonce_odr in a COMDAT the symbol collector does not read, and `_ZN8WithInitC1Ev` is the *implicit* default constructor of a class with a member initialiser, which cxx1 emits as a function and clang inlines away entirely. Nothing this case is about produces a name: it is six legal shapes standing beside six refusals, and what it measures is that they still compile and still print what clang prints.
x86_64-windows  The same, and only one name of the three reaches this target: `?twice@S@@QEBAHXZ`, for the same COMDAT reason. Every other name agrees.
arm64-darwin  The same one name with Mach-O's leading underscore, `__ZNK1S5twiceEv`.
